From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:46:41 -0400
Subject: privacy: tracker-free defaults, one Privacy block in settings

The defaults docs/PRIVACY.md promises become registered preference
defaults: third-party cookies blocked in normal windows, HTTPS-First
balanced mode on, no web service asked about navigation errors, quiet
notification and location prompts, search suggestions off. Global Privacy
Control gets a local-state preference (on) that turns Chromium's own
GlobalPrivacyControlForce feature on where chrome://flags become switches,
so Sec-GPC: 1 and navigator.globalPrivacyControl follow. chrome://settings/
stedding gains a Privacy block, one row per preference, the protective side
on (docs/features/privacy.md Q1-Q8, ADR 0017).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 3, R6-26; PRIVACY.md's to-do table.
Removable when: Chromium ships these defaults, or a build flag sets them.
